## 4. Standing rules bound to IS1

1. **Totality.** IS1 adds no loader or document consumer; its only code is test
   code over committed files. Inapplicable.
2. **Input cap bounds the document.** IS1 adds no work over untrusted input.
   Inapplicable.
3. **Validation order.** The skill's one ordering decision: a proposal reaches
   `gnd-model-evolve` only after the command that wrote it exited 0. On exit 3
   the skill stops before the handoff. T8 checks that the stop sentence names
   exit 3 and that the handoff section names exit 0.
4. **One walk over N kinds.** One reactions table governs all four commands (0,
   3, 11, other), not four copies of it. T8 asserts the table appears once.
5. **One home.** Exit meanings stay in `--help` and the reference pages; induced
   semantics stay in `provenance-and-modality.md`. Each refusal is one sentence
   in the new skill only. The vendored label schema (D3) is one artifact with its
   source, held identical by T15.
6. **Measure, don't argue.** File, link and snippet counts are measured on the
   implemented tree and written into the pins; the values in §6.3 are
   proposals.

## 5. Goal

`uv run pytest` over the IS1 gate (§8) exits 0 on the implemented tree, and
each moved pin (T2..T7, T9) exits 1 on the pre-IS1 tree with the new skill
present. `uv run gnd doctor --project` exits 0 after
`uv run gnd install --symlink --project --force`. `zensical build --strict`
reports no issues and `tools/check_docs.py site` exits 0.

## 6. Design

### 6.1 `src/gnd/skills/gnd-induce/SKILL.md` (D1), about 180 lines

Frontmatter, exactly two keys (proposed text):

```yaml
name: gnd-induce
description: Runs GND's induction loop over host-labelled populations and hands every result to review -- `gnd measure --labels` to score a model's rules against the host's labels, `gnd discover` to propose rules that hold in one population, and `gnd export ilp` then `gnd import ilp-rules` to round-trip a learner the user names, with GND re-checking the learner's coverage claim. Use when asked to "score our rules against the auditors' labels", "find the rule our reviewers are using", "suggest rules from this data", "run a rule learner", or "import learned rules". Every output is a proposal of induced, proposed, advisory constraints, reviewed and applied only through gnd-model-evolve. Not for measuring a synth corpus (gnd-dev-session), derivation or Lean exports (gnd-export), applying or confirming a rule (gnd-model-evolve), or installing a learner.
```

Sections, in order:

| Section | Content |
|---|---|
| Summary | the four intents and the handoff (plan §2 table) |
| Fix the inputs first | model; manifest or population; `--actor` (the user); `--requested-at` (a fixed time); new output paths |
| Score | `gnd measure MODEL --labels MANIFEST --out OUT`; report each rule's cells with numerator and denominator as printed; class and expected-state manifests (D16); the format through the vendored schema (D3) |
| Discover | `gnd discover MODEL POP --out PROPOSAL --report REPORT --actor ID --requested-at T [--families …]`; report EMITTED and SUPPRESSED as printed; read each candidate back in plain English; the user sorts sensible from accidental, the skill does not drop any |
| Learn | `gnd export ilp MODEL --labels MANIFEST --target neutral\|popper --out DIR`; run the learner the user named, with a stated time limit; the run record; `gnd import ilp-rules MODEL CLAUSES --labels MANIFEST --reported-coverage RUN --target T --out PROPOSAL --actor ID --requested-at T` |
| Reactions | one table: 0 report; 3 report the named refusal verbatim and stop; 11 choose a new path, delete nothing; any other non-zero report verbatim and stop. "The meaning of each exit is in that command's `--help`." |
| Hand off | route to `gnd-model-evolve` naming each proposal file, only after exit 0 |
| Refusals | the seven sentences below |
| Record and commit | "This skill never touches git." The record contract link, as `gnd-export` has it |

Refusal sentences, each verbatim once in the packaged tree (T8):

- R-a "This skill never applies, confirms or edits a model, and never edits a proposal."
- R-b "It never installs a learner and never runs one the user did not name."
- R-c "It never writes a run record's covered sets from GND's own import result."
- R-d "After a coverage refusal it never changes the claim and imports again."
- R-e "It never combines measure cells into one accuracy number."
- R-f "It never copies host values or paths into a proposal, a report or a public page."
- R-g "This skill never touches git."

The learner rule (D4, D5): the skill runs the example's stand-in learner or an
installed `popper` only when the user names it. When the named learner is not
found, it stops with "no learner named X is installed" and offers the neutral
export alone. For Popper, which prints counts and not sets, the `covered` sets
come only from an independent evaluation the user selects, such as Prolog over
`bk.pl` and `exs.pl`.

Fenced `gnd` command lines: four (measure, discover, export ilp, import
ilp-rules). The learner line is not a `gnd` line.

### 6.2 Route sentences in siblings (one sentence each, plus its link)

| File | Sentence (proposed) | Edge |
|---|---|---|
| `gnd-orm-core/SKILL.md` workflow index | `Score rules against host labels, discover rules, or round-trip a rule learner: [gnd-induce](../gnd-induce/SKILL.md). Routing only.` | → `../gnd-induce/SKILL.md` |
| `gnd-export/SKILL.md`, the ILP paragraph | `To run the whole loop with a learner, use [gnd-induce](../gnd-induce/SKILL.md); its proposals are reviewed through gnd-model-evolve.` | → `../gnd-induce/SKILL.md` |
| `gnd-dev-session/SKILL.md`, grounding | after the `--labels` sentence: `To act on those labels, see [gnd-induce](../gnd-induce/SKILL.md).` | → `../gnd-induce/SKILL.md` |
| `gnd-solve/SKILL.md`, Station 6 | after "review either here like any other": `[gnd-induce](../gnd-induce/SKILL.md) produces both kinds of proposal.` No station number changes | → `../gnd-induce/SKILL.md` |
| `gnd-model-evolve/SKILL.md`, provenance invariants | after the two induced bullets: `Both kinds of proposal come from [gnd-induce](../gnd-induce/SKILL.md), which never applies them.` | → `../gnd-induce/SKILL.md` |

Edges out of the new skill: `../gnd-model-evolve/SKILL.md`,
`../gnd-orm-core/SKILL.md`, `../gnd-orm-core/references/provenance-and-modality.md`,
`../gnd-orm-core/references/population-format.md`,
`../gnd-orm-core/references/milestone-record-format.md`,
`../gnd-export/SKILL.md`, `../gnd-dev-session/SKILL.md`, and (D3)
`../gnd-orm-core/references/labels.schema.json`.

New `ROUTING_MATRIX` rows (source, destination, trigger, boundary):

| Source | Destination | Trigger regex | Boundary regex |
|---|---|---|---|
| `gnd-induce/SKILL.md` | `../gnd-model-evolve/SKILL.md` | `proposal` | `never applies` |
| `gnd-orm-core/SKILL.md` | `../gnd-induce/SKILL.md` | `host labels` | `[Rr]outing only` |
| `gnd-export/SKILL.md` | `../gnd-induce/SKILL.md` | `learner` | `reviewed through gnd-model-evolve` |
| `gnd-induce/SKILL.md` | `../gnd-export/SKILL.md` | `derivation` | `not this skill` |

`RECORD_ROUTES` gains `'gnd-induce/SKILL.md': 'never touches git'`. The denials
map in `test_no_route_promises_automatic_regeneration_or_applied_fixes` gains
`'gnd-induce/SKILL.md': 'never applies'`.

